# Line endings are LF in the index and LF in every working tree.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its system gitconfig, which
# checks these files out as CRLF. Biome formats to LF, so on Windows every
# file then reads as a whole-file reformat and a real error drowns in the
# noise. eol=lf overrides core.autocrlf whatever a given machine sets, so
# local `npm run check` matches CI.
#
# It also keeps .sh hooks runnable: a CR on the shebang line is "bad
# interpreter".
#
# text=auto still detects binary files (the PNGs) and leaves them untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
